MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lead With Your Heart felt like my strongest next choice because its vocal harmonies fit what I enjoyed about The New Old Fashioned.",
    "Forte and You Should Dream also felt relevant because group vocals interest me, even though I only wanted to try one album this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect to my older listening, but I am not looking for holiday music now; a country Christmas album feels even further from my current interest.",
    "Movie songs and a greatest-hits collection do not give me the same reason to expect the vocal harmonies I want. Together leaves me unsure whether it fits."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My several Christmas interactions happened close together during the holidays, so they do not mean I want Christmas albums throughout the year.",
    "An appealing singer or a vocal album is only part of the match: solo standards, movie songs and Celtic group vocals are not equally appealing to me today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My more recent interest in The New Old Fashioned matters more to this visit than the older cluster of Christmas listening.",
    "I rarely choose something unless the connection feels strong, so finding several albums somewhat appealing still leads me to pick only Lead With Your Heart."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in vocal harmonies but gave too much weight to older holiday listening and broader vocal similarities."
}
